    "u2u": "u2u.png",
    "u2u2": "u2u2.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "Data/Item/u2u.OZJ (32x64: a deep blue lacquered shaft and spiked head, gold rings and an orange thread) on 360 triangles, u2u2.OZJ (16x16, a blue streak on black) on 120. Decoded from MuMain with pipeline/decode_texture.py.",
  "material_overrides": {
    "steel": {
      "roughness": 0.45
    }
  },
  "material_overrides_note": "As the Devias staves': steel's own 0.2 mirrors the grass.",
  "glow": {
    "u2u2": {
      "pulse": [
        0.0,
        -1.1
      ]
    }
  },
  "glow_note": "`case MODEL_CHAOS_LIGHTNING_STAFF`: BlendMesh 1, BlendMeshLight = (rand()%11)*0.1 (ZzzObject.cpp:5234-5237) -- texture 1, u2u2's blue streaks, drawn added at a brightness rolled each frame from 0.0 to 1.0: the staff's lightning flickers. A negative pulse base is the renderer's per-frame roll, (rand()%10)*0.1 times -base (renderer.cpp's Gorgon flicker), so -1.1 rolls 0.0 to 0.99, MU's eleven steps folded into ten. Not here: the BITMAP_SHINY+1 and BITMAP_LIGHT sprites MU hangs on its light bones when held (ZzzCharacter.cpp:10292-10310), a client effect. The streaks ride twelve Box bones that slide 12-26 units through MU's 6-key action 0, which a rigid held item does not play; built at key 0.",
  "rig_note": "No .rig.json, as on Staff06: a rigid weapon needs only MU's geometry at action 0 key 0, which the .obj is, and borrowing the player's motion by bone name is how Staff06's vertices flew off.",
  "inventory_note": "MU turns it in the bag to (0, 0, 205) (ZzzInventory.cpp:9204); the bag here has no per-item angle.",
  "material_note": "The body (360 triangles on u2u) is a deep blue lacquered metal shaft and spiked head with gold rings -- steel. The streaks' 120 triangles are the glow part and wear no material here; their island rows keep steel for the bake only.",
